# Line endings are the repository's decision, not the checkout's.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout gets CRLF (git's `core.autocrlf`
# does it on the way out), while Prettier is configured for LF — so
# `npm run check` reports EVERY file as unformatted on Windows. A command
# that answers "no" whether or not anything is wrong is a command whose
# answer stops being read, and the next real formatting mistake then shows
# up in CI instead. That happened twice before this file existed.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf`: git decides what is text, and text is checked out
# with LF everywhere. What is stored has always been LF; only the checkout
# changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must not touch. Detection is good but not perfect, and a
# font or an icon ZIP that gets "normalised" is a corrupt file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
